{"question_id": "V2-dev-RPT-fa-T2-001", "approach": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "approach_base": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "flags": {}, "setting": "fa-fa", "q_lang": "fa", "d_lang": "fa", "answer_text": "86 درصد از آگهی‌ها به‌صورت رایگان منتشر شده‌اند؛ یعنی از 139.7 میلیون آگهی منتشرشده، حدود 120 میلیون آگهی رایگان بوده است.", "abstained": false, "evidence_chars": 14954, "llm_calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 6416, "completion_tokens": 54, "llm_wall_ms": 2700.5, "latency_ms": 3802.7, "reader_ms": 3802.5, "failed_calls": 0, "error": null, "ts": "2026-11-10T16:55:01", "models": {"chat": "openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}, "split": "dev", "trace": {"lc": {"arm": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "l_tok": 32000, "pack_sha256": "a42da6becc993ff8ae75b7fbdac7e7119d9972d3197344ce992bc516bbdda747", "info": {"budget_chars": 79131, "docs": [{"doc": "C.divar_annual-report_1400.fa", "doc_chars": 14926, "shown": 14926, "ranges": 1, "whole": true}], "gold_units": 2, "gold_units_retained": 2, "gold_docs_shown": 1}, "provider": "Together", "done_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_usd": 0.0009894}}, "meta": {"identity": {"experiment_id": "s4-posthoc-lc", "question_id": "V2-dev-RPT-fa-T2-001", "pool_id": "RPT-fa", "method": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "options": {"flags": {}, "variants_version": "variants-v2", "l_tok": 32000}, "reader": {"chat": "openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash", "chat_digest": "openrouter"}, "replicate": 0, "setting": "fa-fa", "rid": "954578844c84a2b839b4"}, "answer_format": "v2_single", "answer_num_predict": 256, "answer_messages_sha256": "a42da6becc993ff8ae75b7fbdac7e7119d9972d3197344ce992bc516bbdda747"}}
{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T1-001", "approach": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "approach_base": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "answer_text": "Faraday explains that the cup forms because a regular ascending current of air, produced by the candle's own heat, plays on all sides of the candle and keeps the exterior cool, so only the inner part melts (Lecture I, \"A Candle: The Flame\").\n\n- The heat of the candle creates an upward current of air that cools the sides of the wax or tallow, keeping the edge much cooler than the part within (Lecture I).\n- The part within melts from the flame running down the wick, while the outside does not melt, leaving a cup (Lecture I).\n- If the current is disturbed in one direction, the cup becomes lop-sided and the fluid runs over, causing guttering (Lecture I).\n- No fuel would serve for a candle that cannot form this cup, except material like Irish bogwood, which holds its own fuel like a sponge (Lecture I).\n- Irregularly shaped candles, such as fluted ones, are bad burners because they cannot form the nicely-formed edge of the cup (Lecture I).", "abstained": false, "evidence_chars": 142943, "llm_calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 32477, "completion_tokens": 220, "llm_wall_ms": 3844.1, "latency_ms": 3848.5, "reader_ms": 3846.7, "failed_calls": 0, "error": null, "ts": "2026-11-10T16:55:05", "models": {"chat": "openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}, "split": "dev", "trace": {"lc": {"arm": "LC-GOLD-DOCS", "l_tok": 32000, "pack_sha256": "a6aa2bedad5489266ac704df338a1df5096d3882ee1f1113dd1bafad2c27e187", "info": {"budget_chars": 142900, "docs": [{"doc": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", "doc_chars": 220892, "shown": 142900, "ranges": 1, "whole": false}], "gold_units": 1, "gold_units_retained": 1, "gold_docs_shown": 1}, "provider": "Together", "done_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_usd": 0.00497387}}, "meta": {"identity": {"experiment_id": "s4-posthoc-lc", "question_id